WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.434
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.467
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.834
Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:13.000
Well, guys, after more than half
a century as Prince of Wales,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
73-year-old Prince Charles
has officially become

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.100
King Charles III.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.667
Yeah, he's now the oldest person
ever to assume

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.601
the British throne, but weirdly,

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:24.567
he's still too young
to be a U.S. president.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:27.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.667
Interesting. Interesting fact.
-A little bit.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:32.501
-King Charles was previously
known as the Prince of Wales,

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.234
and now his son, William,
will take the title.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.000
I don't want to be that guy,
but I get the feeling

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.868
that there's a little nepotism
involved.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:43.000
Some news from here
in the United States.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.968
A new poll found that
in a potential 2024 matchup,

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:50.067
President Biden has a six-point
lead on former president Trump.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.434
Yeah.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.601
The poll says,
8% Biden, 2% Trump,

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.367
90% other.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.501
-Wow.
-Anyone.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.934
That's right. Trump is
six points behind Biden.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.434
That's right.
Trump was so upset,

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.033
he had to dry his eyes with
Israel's nuclear secrets.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.501
People were talking about this
last night.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.534
It was the first NFL game
of the season,

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:22.901
and the Buffalo Bills
beat the L.A. Rams, 31-10.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.767
-The big story was Bills star
Von Miller's haircut.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.901
Did you see this?
Take a look at this.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:35.400
It's a bold statement.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.534
And the statement is,
"elevator up."

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.167
I guess he went into the barber

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.701
and asked for
the PlayStation button.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:47.200
Seriously, the options on the
barbershop wall must have been

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.667
the business card
from "Squid Game."

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.434
Did you guys see this?
Before last night's game,

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:56.067
the new trailer for "Black Adam"
starring Dwayne Johnson

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.300
debuted in the stadium.
It was cool.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.601
But I was a little surprised at

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:01.133
who they got to
voice the trailer.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.400
Did you see it? Check this out.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.100
-Hi. I'm Vin Diesel,
and this is Dwayne Johnson.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.133
Maybe you remember he used to be
part of our family,

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:14.200
but then he left that family,
and you never leave family.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.901
Now, he's hanging out with
all these super people.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.868
I get you could say
they're like a different family.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:22.467
This helmet guy
is like the daddy.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.534
Smoke lady is the mommy.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:28.100
Wing guy, he's a friend,
but he's such a close friend

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.000
that they call him Uncle,
so he's family.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.467
I guess he found a new family.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:36.801
Go see it in theaters,
where you'll also see a trailer

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:40.501
for "Fast X,"
another movie about family.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:45.434
Trailers are like the babies of
movies, which makes them family.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:48.400
-Very interesting.
Great trailer. It looks good.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.434
-I'll go see it.
-It looks good.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:51.701
-Yeah.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.133
-Hey, guys, I read that
on the new hit show,

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.734
"House of the Dragon," a few of
the main characters are being

00:02:57.734 --> 00:03:01.467
recast as the series jumps
forward about 10 years in time.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:04.067
For instance, the actress who
played the princess is changing

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:07.133
from Milly Alcock
to Emma D'Arcy.

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.901
Yeah. This is true.
And apparently that's not

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.367
the only place where people
are recast to look older.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.901
For instance,
on "Stranger Things," Will is

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.234
being recast as Las Vegas
Raiders owner Mark Davis.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:18.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.868
It's older Will.
-Wow, it's older Will.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.634
-Yeah.
Next, in the Marvel movie, Thor

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.601
is being recast
as Willie Nelson.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.501
[ Laughter ]
The new Thor.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:31.067
Next, "Lord of the Rings: Rings
of Power," Elrond, the half elf,

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.067
is being recast
as Pete Buttigieg.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:37.801
Next up, on "She-Hulk: Attorney
at Law," She-Hulk is being

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.367
recast as Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.934
Next up, going forward,
Harry Styles is being recast

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:46.033
as Elton John.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:49.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.968
You like that?

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.033
Yeah, we love Harry too.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:58.734
Next up on CNN, Anderson Cooper
is being recast as Wolf Blitzer.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:02.834
And finally, on "Euphoria,"
Fez is being recast

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.000
as Pope Francis.
And it's just great.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.200
You won't even know
the difference.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.534
It's going to be
exciting to watch.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.133
It'll be fun to see.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.267
Get this, guys.
I saw that DC Comics has

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:16.934
revealed that the Joker's
real name is Jack Oswald White.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.367
Yeah, pretty interesting.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.767
So I thought it would be fun
right now if some of us here,

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.367
me, Higgins, the Roots,
reveal our real names

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:24.634
for the first time.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:25.868
I'll go first.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.400
My real name is...

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.968
Devin St. Monroe.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.434
Quest, how about you?

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:33.901
-My real name is...

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:36.133
Bart Tomato.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:39.133
That's cool. Never knew that.
Tariq, how about you?

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.801
-My real name is...

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:43.934
Spunk. Chuck Spunk.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:46.334
-That's cool.
Higgins, how about you?

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:47.701
-My real name is...

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:49.367
Thomas Scrotum Jr.

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.200
-Okay.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.000
James, how about you?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.334
-My real name?
[ Suspenseful music plays

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.167
You don't want to know
my real name.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:03.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.300
Okay. How much time do you got?

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:10.267
I wasn't like my other friends
growing up.

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:13.968
While they were playing tag, I
was in the woods looking at bugs

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.934
and trying to figure out
how trees grow.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:19.767
Sounds crazy?

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.167
Well, welcome to my life.

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:27.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:30.334
-Wow, that's his name?

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.267
-I -- That's --
That's pretty cool, James.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.467
So, what is your real name?

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.734
[ Cymbal crashes ]

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.467
-Thomas Scrotum Sr.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:42.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:45.767
-Unbelievable.
This is unbelievable.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.767
-Daddy!
-Well, we got our real names.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.667
Moving on, moving on,
moving on, moving on.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:54.234
[ Laughter ]
Please.

00:05:54.234 --> 00:05:55.767
-Too many balls in the air.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:58.067
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:00.367
I don't want to leave anyone
hanging. Let's go with the rest.

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:05.400
Some business news -- Uber Eats
just announced that they're

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.167
going to start testing out
driverless delivery.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.767
Driverless delivery cars
are incredible.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.100
They're even programmed to say,

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.701
[Robotic voice] "Wow, two orders
from Popeyes in one day."

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:16.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.868
"What's going on, Carl?"

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.968
[ Normal voice ] And finally,
passengers on a Carnival cruise

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:23.467
woke up to a rough scene
after plumbing issues

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.133
caused some flooding.
Look at this.

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:30.667
Wow. Yeah.

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:31.801
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:33.400
It's not good
when you have to use

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.033
the lifeboats inside the ship.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.567 --> 00:06:38.167
Of course, the captain tried to
spin it.

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:40.200
He was like,
"Did we say six water slides?

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.634
We meant seven." Yeah.

